# An exported class is a route whose steps are its public methods, each called by the entry. `Source.read` is a call
# into the family of `Source`, whose members along the method resolution order are `Buffered`, `Feed` and `Tape`: it
# runs one of the overrides that family holds, a choice between them (`Buffered` has no `read` of its own and runs the
# base's body, the dispatch's own arrow). The Source the caller calls it on, a value from beyond, is what each override
# runs on; the base's own body does not read it. Every `read` gives bytes, of no type of the code's: what an override
# gives goes back to the dispatch that ran it.
route reading.feeds.Source
step Source()/Source.read
step Source()/Source.read/Feed.read
step Source()/Source.read/Tape.read

line entry > Source()/Source.read call
line Source > Source()/Source.read/Feed.read value
line Source > Source()/Source.read/Tape.read value
line Source()/Source.read/Feed.read > Source()/Source.read back
line Source()/Source.read/Tape.read > Source()/Source.read back

home Source Source()

side entry left

# each override takes a value of its own class from beyond, and the Source ends at the border of the dispatch
